{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ורדפו מכם חמשה", :translit "urdefu mikhem chamisha", :gloss "and shall pursue from you five"} {:he "חלשים שבכם", :translit "chlashim shebakhem", :gloss "the weak among you"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ורדפו מכם חמשה", :b "חלשים שבכם"}], :frame {:text "Rashi on Leviticus 26:8, citing the Sifra on this verse, explains that the five pursuers are the weakest among the people — even the frail will chase multitudes.", :sources ["Rashi on Leviticus 26:8" "Sifra Bechukotai 6:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "רבבה", :translit "rivavah", :gloss "ten thousand"} {:he "אחותנו את היי לאלפי רבבה", :translit "achotenu at hayi le'alfei rivavah", :gloss "our sister, may you be for thousands of ten-thousands"} {:he "רבבה כצמח השדה", :translit "rivavah ketzemach hasadeh", :gloss "ten thousand like the growth of the field"} {:he "ושנים יניסו רבבה", :translit "ushenayim yanisu rivavah", :gloss "and two shall put to flight ten thousand"} {:he "רבבה ירדופו", :translit "rivavah yerdofu", :gloss "ten thousand they shall pursue"} {:he "שהתפללו עליה שיהיו זרעה מאותם שנאמר בהם רבבה כצמח ורבבה ירדופו", :translit "shehitpalelu aleiha sheyihyu zar'ah me'otem she'ne'emar bahem rivavah ketzemach verivavah yerdofu", :gloss "that they prayed over her that her seed would be from those about whom it is said 'rivavah like the growth' and 'rivavah they shall pursue'"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["אחותנו את היי לאלפי רבבה" "רבבה כצמח השדה" "ושנים יניסו רבבה" "רבבה ירדופו"]}], :frame {:text "The word 'rivavah' appears in four verses: Ruth 4:2 ('achotenu at hayi le'alfei rivavah' addressed to Ruth), and three others. Boaz's prayer in Ruth 4:11-12 that Ruth be like Rachel and Leah includes the imagery of 'ketzemach hasadeh' (like the growth of the field). The Ba'al HaTurim connects the 'rivavah' of military pursuit in Leviticus 26:8 with Boaz's prayer for Ruth's seed.", :sources ["Ruth 4:11" "Ruth 4:12" "Leviticus 26:8"]}}], :arit